// Functional record update `{r | f = e}`. The frontend admits it, and the go
// reference REFUSES it by name: only the python and typescript tiers emit it
// today (docs/records.md §6, "lift it into a helper fn instead").
//
// Not a byte-agreement case, so it cannot live in the tier's CORPUS. The
// line-coverage gate drives both halves over it here: the reference's raise in
// `_go_v3_expr`, and the port's `<<UNSUPPORTED-EXPR:record_update>>` marker.
type R = { x: Int, y: Int }

fn bump(r: R) -> R { return {r | x = r.x + 1} }
